SUMMARY:Of Times There Were Before
DESCRIPTION:Directed by Eshan Sharma\n\nOf Times There Were Before is a p
 ortrait of Romila Thapar\, one of the world’s most influential histori
 ans and public intellectuals. At ninety-four\, having lived through much
  of the making of modern India\, she stands at an unusual distance from 
 the past she has spent a lifetime studying. The film began with a simple
  question: who is the person behind the historian’s name? Shot at her 
 home in New Delhi\, it is an attempt to encounter Thapar beyond the auth
 ority of her work and the public image built around it. What emerges is 
 a portrait of a life still in conversation with its own time.\n\nhttps:/
 /www.themoviedb.org/movie/1792337
URL:https://www.themoviedb.org/movie/1792337
TRANSP:TRANSPARENT
END:VEVENT
