SUMMARY:Tin Castle
DESCRIPTION:Directed by Alexander Murphy\n\nAlong a long-forgotten road\,
  the O’Reillys live in a rundown trailer stranded in the middle of the
  fields. Pa’\, Lisa\, and their ten children weather the seasons in th
 eir tin castle\, heirs to a way of life on borrowed time. Under threat o
 f eviction\, their tenuous balance falters\, yet – steadfast in their 
 tradition – they resist. The children laugh\, the dogs bark\, the trai
 ler holds on – but for how long?\n\nhttps://www.themoviedb.org/movie/1
 666146
URL:https://www.themoviedb.org/movie/1666146
TRANSP:TRANSPARENT
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:movie-1584595@doc-radar
DTSTAMP:20261109T145339Z
DTSTART;VALUE=DATE:20261120
DTEND;VALUE=DATE:20261121
SUMMARY:Zahir
DESCRIPTION:Directed by Julien Nadiras\n\nWhen Katherine Choong suggested
  to her friend Éline Le Menestrel that they tackle the Zahir\, a classi
 c route in the Swiss Alps and a demanding gem of the Wendenstöcke\, Él
 ine agreed... on one condition: that they only use sustainable transport
  to get to the foot of the wall.  As the days passed suspended on the ro
 ck\, they realized the scale of the challenge: intense commitment\, tiny
  holds\, accumulated fatigue from cycling... every movement became a cha
 llenge.  Between motivation and euphoria\, perseverance and doubt\, woul
 d Katherine and Éline manage to reach their Zahir\, that summit where a
 udacity and wild beauty come together?\n\nhttps://www.themoviedb.org/mov
 ie/1584595
URL:https://www.themoviedb.org/movie/1584595
TRANSP:TRANSPARENT
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:movie-1782278@doc-radar
DTSTAMP:20261109T145339Z
DTSTART;VALUE=DATE:20261120
DTEND;VALUE=DATE:20261121
SUMMARY:Obsession: The Beryl Burton Story
DESCRIPTION:Directed by Stuart Pollitt\n\nA documentary about Britain’s
  greatest athlete. Undefeated for 25 years\, Leeds-born amateur cyclist 
 Beryl Burton won seven World Championships\, beat men’s records and tr
 ansformed women’s sport; all while working on a Yorkshire rhubarb farm
 . Through unseen archive\, letters and intimate interviews\, the film ex
 plores the glory of her achievements and the cost of her obsession\, par
 ticularly on her relationship with her daughter Denise\, who followed he
 r into competitive cycling.\n\nhttps://www.themoviedb.org/movie/1782278
URL:https://www.themoviedb.org/movie/1782278
TRANSP:TRANSPARENT
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:movie-1778412@doc-radar
DTSTAMP:20261109T145339Z
DTSTART;VALUE=DATE:20261120
DTEND;VALUE=DATE:20261121
SUMMARY:Inside the Mountain
DESCRIPTION:Directed by Jack Homan\n\nIn 1988\, Paul Eastwood and his cli
 mbing partner became the first men to free-climb Britain's deepest open 
 cave shaft\, rising from within the UK's largest underground chamber and
  traversing around its highest unbroken waterfall\, three times the heig
 ht of Niagara falls. The iconic route will have gone unrepeated for almo
 st 40 years. Decades later a new team of climbers\, Olympian Molly Thomp
 son-Smith and legend Steve McClure\, will tackle the climb once again\,
  hoping to join the few who have ever free-climbed the route.\n\nhttps:/
 /www.themoviedb.org/movie/1778412
URL:https://www.themoviedb.org/movie/1778412
TRANSP:TRANSPARENT
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:movie-1805666@doc-radar
DTSTAMP:20261109T145339Z
DTSTART;VALUE=DATE:20261120
DTEND;VALUE=DATE:20261121
SUMMARY:75 Seconds
DESCRIPTION:Directed by Marco Tribelhorn\n\nOn a foggy March evening in N
 orway\, freeskier Jacob Wester triggers an avalanche and is swept off a 
 cliff. For 75 seconds\, he fights for his life inside a roaring mass of 
 snow\, while his wife Sofia waits in silence below. This is an account o
 f chaos\, fear\, and hope inside an avalanche.\n\nhttps://www.themoviedb
 .org/movie/1805666
URL:https://www.themoviedb.org/movie/1805666
TRANSP:TRANSPARENT
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:movie-1807374@doc-radar
DTSTAMP:20261109T145339Z
DTSTART;VALUE=DATE:20261120
DTEND;VALUE=DATE:20261121
SUMMARY:Big Jim: An American on Everest
DESCRIPTION:Directed by Jim Aikman\n\n“Big Jim” Whittaker (1929-2026)
  was a legendary Pacific Northwest mountaineer who became the first Amer
 ican to summit Mount Everest on May 1\, 1963. This short documentary exp
 lores his “brotherhood of the rope” with his twin brother\, Lou\, as
  well as Nawang Gombu Sherpa\, his Everest climbing partner and lifelong
  friend. Featuring rarely seen 16mm footage from the 1963 Everest Expedi
 tion\, archival images from the Whittaker family collection\, and interv
 iews filmed in Jim’s late 80s\, the film is both an intimate portrait 
 of an extraordinary life and a celebration of the adventurous spirit tha
 t helped define a generation of climbers.\n\nhttps://www.themoviedb.org/
 movie/1807374
URL:https://www.themoviedb.org/movie/1807374
TRANSP:TRANSPARENT
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:movie-1625174@doc-radar
DTSTAMP:20261109T145339Z
DTSTART;VALUE=DATE:20261120
DTEND;VALUE=DATE:20261121
SUMMARY:Glacier's Requiem
DESCRIPTION:Directed by Saddiq Abubakar\n\nIn isolation on Iceland’s Sn
 æfellsnes Peninsula\, Nigerian-born modular synthesis artist Colloboh t
 ransforms glacial and oceanic recordings into sonic compositions; uncove
 ring a dialogue between ice and sea that reshapes his understanding of c
 onsciousness\, ecological collapse\, and humanity’s place within both.
 \n\nhttps://www.themoviedb.org/movie/1625174
URL:https://www.themoviedb.org/movie/1625174
TRANSP:TRANSPARENT
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:movie-1809154@doc-radar
DTSTAMP:20261109T145339Z
DTSTART;VALUE=DATE:20261120
DTEND;VALUE=DATE:20261121
SUMMARY:Framed
DESCRIPTION:Directed by Bernardo Giménez\n\nSiebe Vanhee sets out to ons
 ight Voie Petit\, a brutal 12-pitch 8a+ line at 3\,500m on the Grand Cap
 ucin\, completely alone - no partner\, no static ropes\, just lead rope-
 solo technique and a drone circling above. But even a solo mission as a 
 professional climber has a crew: a manager on the phone\, a sponsor wait
 ing for footage\, a director on the glacier\, and Vanhee himself playing
  climber\, cameraman and storyteller all at once\, selfie-interviewing h
 is own exhaustion pitch by pitch.\n\nhttps://www.themoviedb.org/movie/18
 09154
URL:https://www.themoviedb.org/movie/1809154
TRANSP:TRANSPARENT
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:movie-1809835@doc-radar
DTSTAMP:20261109T145339Z
DTSTART;VALUE=DATE:20261120
DTEND;VALUE=DATE:20261121
SUMMARY:The Hillbilly Scientist
DESCRIPTION:Directed by Paul Mellor\n\nWhile modern running has evolved t
 oward sleek curation\, optimisation\, and commercialisation\, Lazarus La
 ke has spent 50 years designing formats with an unapologetic\, honest di
 fficulty. The Hillbilly Scientist reveals that Laz’s cruellest courses
  are rooted in a deeply scientific understanding of human psychology and
  physical limits. This is the only official documentary dedicated to the
  creator of the Barkley Marathons and Big’s Backyard Ultra. Filmed ove
 r more than a year\, it reveals the man behind the myth through never-be
 fore-seen footage\, exclusive testimonials\, and exceptional access to L
 az’s world.\n\nhttps://www.themoviedb.org/movie/1809835
URL:https://www.themoviedb.org/movie/1809835
TRANSP:TRANSPARENT
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:movie-1813716@doc-radar
DTSTAMP:20261109T145339Z
DTSTART;VALUE=DATE:20261120
DTEND;VALUE=DATE:20261121
SUMMARY:Rongo
DESCRIPTION:Directed by Finlay Woods\n\nWith plenty of powder to go aroun
 d\, un-ridden waves rolling into secret golden beaches\, and local chara
 cters to greet you with a smile\, six professional athletes make the mos
 t of every moment during an action-packed adventure through Aotearoa\, N
 Z!\n\nhttps://www.themoviedb.org/movie/1813716
URL:https://www.themoviedb.org/movie/1813716
TRANSP:TRANSPARENT
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:movie-1650016@doc-radar
DTSTAMP:20261109T145339Z
DTSTART;VALUE=DATE:20261120
DTEND;VALUE=DATE:20261121
SUMMARY:Same Sun - Cycling through Africa
DESCRIPTION:Directed by Fabienne Engel\n\nThe story of Wiebke Lühmann's 
 journey from Freiburg to the Cape of Good Hope. Honest\, raw\, and close
  to the inner and outer challenges of a 430-day bicycle trip. Her journe
 y takes her through 22 countries\, Sahara storms\, the rain season\, the
  Congo Basin\, and the deserts of Namibia. What begins as a search for i
 ndependence becomes an intimate exploration of identity.\n\nhttps://www.
 themoviedb.org/movie/1650016
URL:https://www.themoviedb.org/movie/1650016
TRANSP:TRANSPARENT
END:VEVENT
