DTSTAMP:20261109T145339Z
DTSTART;VALUE=DATE:20261120
DTEND;VALUE=DATE:20261121
SUMMARY:Aldo's Raptor Roundup
DESCRIPTION:Directed by Neil Losin\n\nSix-year old Aldo spends an excitin
 g weekend banding migrating raptors in Cape May\, New Jersey with his fr
 iend John\, a volunteer bander with the Cape May Raptor Banding Project.
 \n\nhttps://www.themoviedb.org/movie/1806591
URL:https://www.themoviedb.org/movie/1806591
TRANSP:TRANSPARENT
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:movie-1645388@doc-radar
DTSTAMP:20261109T145339Z
DTSTART;VALUE=DATE:20261120
DTEND;VALUE=DATE:20261121
SUMMARY:The Last of the Lookouts
DESCRIPTION:Directed by Ryan Wilkes\n\nHigh atop Sinkut Mountain in north
 ern British Columbia\, Bart Vanderlinde begins each summer's day the way
  he has for the past nine years: scanning the forest for smoke. He's amo
 ng the last lookout people in the province. Where three hundred lookouts
  once formed an interconnected network across the region\, Bart now ofte
 n keeps watch alone. This is an intimate portrait of a man and a profess
 ion facing obsolescence. The film gives insight into the craft of fire d
 etection while capturing the quiet solitude of a life lived in observati
 on.\n\nhttps://www.themoviedb.org/movie/1645388
URL:https://www.themoviedb.org/movie/1645388
TRANSP:TRANSPARENT
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:movie-1807273@doc-radar
DTSTAMP:20261109T145339Z
DTSTART;VALUE=DATE:20261120
DTEND;VALUE=DATE:20261121
SUMMARY:Beura
DESCRIPTION:Directed by Gregor D. Sinclair\n\nThe tale of the Cailleach B
 heur\, the Celtic goddess of nature\, storms and winter\, is well known 
 to many in the Gàidhealtachd. Said to have carved the mountains and gle
 ns with ice\, and borne the islands like children on her back\, the Cail
 leach disappeared long ago leaving us only with her song – a sad\, cau
 tionary tale. This Gaelic arts project brings music\, film and verse tog
 ether to reimagine Cailleach’s story for the modern era.\n\nhttps://ww
 w.themoviedb.org/movie/1807273
URL:https://www.themoviedb.org/movie/1807273
TRANSP:TRANSPARENT
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:movie-1567157@doc-radar
DTSTAMP:20261109T145339Z
DTSTART;VALUE=DATE:20261120
DTEND;VALUE=DATE:20261121
SUMMARY:A Mystical Ornithology
DESCRIPTION:Directed by Jeremy Seifert\n\nImmersed in the songs of blue j
 ays\, yellow-throated warblers\, and red-shouldered hawks on his forty-s
 ix-acre farm in rural South Carolina\, acclaimed poet and ornithologist 
 J. Drew Lanham exchanges calls with the birds that stop over at his home
  during their seasonal migrations. For Drew\, these creatures are gods\,
  transcendent beings who summon a response of reverence. Reverberating w
 ith sound\, music\, light\, and ethereal cinematic expression\, A Mystic
 al Ornithology weaves a kinetic texture for the senses and invites you i
 nto a poetic evocation of the paradox of love and grief within the chang
 ing nature of the seasons.\n\nhttps://www.themoviedb.org/movie/1567157
URL:https://www.themoviedb.org/movie/1567157
TRANSP:TRANSPARENT
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:movie-1776026@doc-radar
DTSTAMP:20261109T145339Z
DTSTART;VALUE=DATE:20261120
DTEND;VALUE=DATE:20261121
SUMMARY:Borrowed from the Earth
DESCRIPTION:Directed by Zach Johaneson\n\nTells the story of the powerful
  connection between the Blackfeet people and horses\, and how that life-
 giving relationship remains alive today. Throughout their histories\, bo
 th horse and Indigenous people have been corralled - horses by fences\, 
 and Indigenous people onto reservations. Yet centuries-long attempts to 
 subdue both ultimately strengthened the bond between them. Saddle up for
  a visually poetic journey from the origin story of the horse to the mod
 ern day Indian Relay Race. Filmed on the Blackfeet Reservation in Browni
 ng\, Montana.\n\nhttps://www.themoviedb.org/movie/1776026
URL:https://www.themoviedb.org/movie/1776026
TRANSP:TRANSPARENT
END:VEVENT
